</section>

<section id="join"><h2>Joins</h2>
<p>The same 20 most recent orders of a one-day window, each with its customer&rsquo;s name and tier. Every engine was given its own idiom, shown above: a SQL join for PostgreSQL, <code>$lookup</code> for MongoDB, <code>DOCUMENT()</code> for SoliDB and ArangoDB, a record link for SurrealDB.</p><p>This is one of the two series SoliDB loses. At one client PostgreSQL typed answers in 71&nbsp;µs at the median and SoliDB in 80, level with PostgreSQL jsonb; SoliDB&rsquo;s 99th percentile is lower, 86&nbsp;µs against 91. At 32 clients SoliDB serves 68,784 joins a second, 1.56 times PostgreSQL typed&rsquo;s 44,221. The document databases trail far behind: ArangoDB takes 238&nbsp;µs, MongoDB 326 and SurrealDB 613 at one client.</p>
